      "spam": false,
      "value": "I have also had this issue.  It's based on Height to width ratio (arm length basically)\n\nThere Is a slight work around for the time being, however does not work if you are using Leg tracking.\n\nAdjusting your height while in stand mode, set to your actual height.\nSwitch to Sit mode\nAdjust your height again, make it lower.  I go from 5'9\" to 4'10\" because my one avatar has longer legs.  \n\nThis will make your arms reach make length before your actual arms do though, but I feels better to reach the ground, and have the ground in VRchat reach my actual floor (even though Steam's floor is set to my actual floor)\n\nI would love to have a better way to adjust IPD (the thing that scales your perspective based on height x width.)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-01-10T11:22:32.542Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This may be a problem on my end, but in VR it is near impossible for me to pick up stuff off the ground with most of my avatars, I hit my physical ground before I can reach.\nIt'd be a neat idea to have a height based hand collider that'd get bigger the closer you got from the ground so as to make it easier to pick something up.",
